se premium cards\n- If the landlord passes, my teammate gets control\n- It preserves my pairs for potential combinations later\n\nReason:\nI\'m choosing to play **♣K** because it\'s a strong single that puts pressure on the landlord (who only has 5 cards). This forces the landlord to either use a valuable card (2, Ace, or joker) or pass, potentially giving control to my teammate who has 13 cards and needs opportunities to play. Preserving my pairs gives me more flexibility for future plays.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣K"]}'}
